    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30428" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nāsĭdĭus</span></b> ,
		a, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>name of a Roman</i> gens. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> L. Nasidius, <i>a Roman knight</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil.
				7, 8, 24</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>An adherent of Pompey</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 2,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 11, 17,
			3</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nā-sĭdĭānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., Nasidian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					C. 2, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
